# Which files make up each check that .harness/mutations.tsv names, for land.sh:
# one "check<TAB>path" per line. A change to a path replays that check's faults.
failing check: blocks with the FAIL line as feedback	tests/stop-gate.test.sh
4 failures in a row: 4th allows the stop and prints the budget line	tests/stop-gate.test.sh
Write a JWT: denied, value not echoed	tests/guard-secrets.test.sh
check-reviewed: an edited old line fails (append-only)	tests/review.test.sh
ship.sh: stops on red CI with the run's URL; main untouched	tests/ship.test.sh
check-defects: an edited line fails	tests/check-defects.test.sh
replay-faults: a SURVIVED fault exits non-zero	tests/replay-faults.test.sh
harness-metrics: no defects.tsv: escaped defects are NOT FOUND, not 0	tests/harness-metrics.test.sh
install-hooks: the commit-msg hook refuses a message check-commits would fail, with the fix; --no-verify commits	tests/ship.test.sh
ship.sh: a non-PASS review: commits its line with the standard message, stops and shows the verdict	tests/ship.test.sh
ship.sh: a stale index is regenerated and committed before the review, through the commit-msg hook	tests/ship.test.sh
upgrade.sh: writes the pin commit draft (Breaks kept, Decision relabelled Upstream, numbers on Told) and it passes the commit-msg hook	tests/upgrade.test.sh
git-guard: git push in the real working tree is denied, however it is written	tests/git-guard.test.sh
approve-brief.sh: refuses without a terminal and writes nothing; with no brief it says to run /plan	tests/ship.test.sh
review.sh: the input holds the brief and whether its approval matches	tests/review.test.sh
ship.sh: no brief, or an approval that does not match, stops before the review with the exact fix	tests/ship.test.sh
brief-guard: Write, Edit, MultiEdit and NotebookEdit of a *.brief.approved file in the real tree are denied	tests/brief-guard.test.sh
git-guard: a shell command naming a *.brief.approved file in the real tree is denied	tests/brief-guard.test.sh
start-up picture: the brief line says approved with the goal, not approved, changed since it was approved, or none	tests/session-start.test.sh
start-up picture: the last check is this branch's latest CHECKED line, with its failing checks, or none	tests/session-start.test.sh
start-up picture: at most 5 failing checks are named, then and N more	tests/session-start.test.sh
start-up picture: the last review is this branch's latest line in .harness/reviews.tsv, or none	tests/session-start.test.sh
start-up picture: uncommitted changes are counted by kind in one line, or none	tests/session-start.test.sh
start-up picture: the state file's first 10 lines, from .harness/state-file or docs/STATE.md, or none	tests/session-start.test.sh
start-up picture: never more than 15 lines, none longer than 200 characters, a cut line ending in …	tests/session-start.test.sh
session-start: the reviewer's session gets the version line only (no report, no warning)	tests/ship.test.sh
stop-gate: records a check in the event log: FAIL with the failing checks' names, or PASS	tests/stop-gate.test.sh
stop-gate: records only a changed result: the same result again adds no line; PASS after FAIL, FAIL after PASS, or a different set of failing checks adds one	tests/stop-gate.test.sh
land.sh: each stop, with its reason, and each LANDED is a line in .git/harness-kit/events.tsv	tests/ship.test.sh
ship.sh: each stop, with its reason, and each SHIPPED is a line in .git/harness-kit/events.tsv	tests/ship.test.sh
release.sh: a failing check stops it before any push	tests/release.test.sh
harness-metrics: CHECKED lines change no number	tests/harness-metrics.test.sh
